1.	Start.
2.	Read the number of emergency stations and road connections.
3.	Represent each station as a vertex and each road connection as an edge using an adjacency list.
4.	Read the selected source station.
5.	Initialize all stations as unvisited.
6.	Insert the source station into a queue and mark it as visited.
7.	Remove a station from the queue and display it.
8.	Visit all its unvisited neighbouring stations, mark them as visited, and insert them into the queue.
9.	Repeat Steps 7–8 until the queue becomes empty.
10.	Display the BFS traversal order.
11.	Check all stations and list those that remain unvisited as unreachable stations.
12.	Stop.

